WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.563
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:14.833 --> 00:18.375
[ominous music]

3
01:05.042 --> 01:08.042
[ominous music continues]

4
01:15.417 --> 01:18.542
[door creaking]

5
01:20.208 --> 01:22.532
[gasps]

6
01:33.753 --> 01:36.313
[ominous music continues]

7
01:58.167 --> 02:01.042
[chittering]

8
02:02.325 --> 02:04.660
[slurp]

9
02:09.510 --> 02:10.708
[slurp ceases]

10
02:10.792 --> 02:13.334
[birds chirping]

11
02:14.813 --> 02:17.029
[ominous music continues]

12
02:36.625 --> 02:39.703
[music builds up]

13
03:00.583 --> 03:01.925
[music fades out]

14
03:02.009 --> 03:04.524
[crickets chirping]

15
03:08.125 --> 03:09.125
You wanted to see me?

16
03:10.542 --> 03:11.999
I hope you have good news.

17
03:12.083 --> 03:14.458
25 YEARS LATER

18
03:14.542 --> 03:15.542
They're not so good.

19
03:16.958 --> 03:18.333
I need more time, Luisa.

20
03:20.375 --> 03:22.124
That's what you said last year.

21
03:22.208 --> 03:23.625
I know, but…

22
03:25.125 --> 03:27.249
the material isn't ready yet.

23
03:27.333 --> 03:28.958
You've got nothing, right?

24
03:29.042 --> 03:32.482
I do, I just don't know if I wanna get back to horror.

25
03:33.458 --> 03:34.299
Sorry?

26
03:35.375 --> 03:36.333
I'd like to…

27
03:37.375 --> 03:39.333
explore other genres.

28
03:39.917 --> 03:41.875
- To… - [Luisa] Okay.

29
03:44.750 --> 03:45.958
[inhales deeply]

30
03:47.958 --> 03:51.458
"The author who redefined horror in Latin America."

31
03:52.792 --> 03:55.417
"The story that's sweeping bookstores."

32
03:57.417 --> 03:59.791
"Terror has a new name:

33
03:59.875 --> 04:01.291
Mercedes Vega."

34
04:01.375 --> 04:03.499
Yes, I know, Luisa. I know.

35
04:03.583 --> 04:04.440
[Luisa] Then what?

36
04:05.125 --> 04:07.542
Do you want to be a serious writer?

37
04:08.500 --> 04:09.792
Do you want to get awards?

38
04:10.730 --> 04:12.416
[Mercedes] You know it's not that.

39
04:12.500 --> 04:14.333
I just want to…

40
04:15.250 --> 04:17.875
try and do something different.

41
04:18.918 --> 04:20.251
Write something different.

42
04:21.083 --> 04:22.333
Okay, listen to me.

43
04:23.417 --> 04:26.417
Take your time to think this over.

44
04:27.042 --> 04:29.084
As your editor, I wouldn't recommend it.

45
04:30.625 --> 04:33.018
But I'll help you, okay?

46
04:34.199 --> 04:35.041
Thank you.

47
04:35.125 --> 04:38.291
I can delay the book launch by a few months,

48
04:38.375 --> 04:41.583
but I need to present something soon.

49
04:41.667 --> 04:42.834
You can count on that.

50
04:43.792 --> 04:44.633
Oh.

51
04:45.750 --> 04:46.708
I almost forgot.

52
04:52.000 --> 04:53.417
You've got some fan mail.

53
04:55.458 --> 04:58.698
Do people still write letters?

54
04:58.782 --> 04:59.623
[Luisa] Well,

55
05:00.333 --> 05:02.458
there are still some romantics out there.

56
05:03.125 --> 05:04.625
Those are the interesting ones.

57
05:05.792 --> 05:06.667
[Luisa] Coffee?

58
05:07.625 --> 05:08.583
Always.

59
05:10.830 --> 05:11.842
Soon!

60
05:11.926 --> 05:12.875
[chuckles] Okay.

61
05:17.000 --> 05:19.708
[pensive music]

62
05:22.625 --> 05:23.500
[door closes]

63
05:40.333 --> 05:47.266
MERCEDES, I DON'T WANT TO LEAVE THIS WORLD WITHOUT SEEING YOU ONE LAST TIME. DAD

64
05:49.625 --> 05:51.542
[dial tone]

65
05:54.542 --> 05:56.542
[dial tone]

66
05:57.750 --> 05:59.499
- [woman] Hello? - [Mercedes] Hello?

67
05:59.583 --> 06:01.041
[woman] Yeah? Who's this?

68
06:01.125 --> 06:03.289
[Mercedes] It's Mercedes. Mercedes Vega.

69
06:03.373 --> 06:06.291
[woman] Mercedes? I'm surprised. I didn't expected you--

70
06:06.375 --> 06:08.416
[Mercedes] I'm sorry. Who's this?

71
06:08.500 --> 06:10.791
- [woman] It's me. Belén. - [Mercedes] Who?

72
06:10.875 --> 06:13.042
[Belén] Belén, Ana María's daughter.

73
06:14.417 --> 06:15.833
[Mercedes] Oh, right.

74
06:15.917 --> 06:18.541
I'd like to speak to Jaime. Is he available?

75
06:18.625 --> 06:22.041
[Belén] He… he can't talk right now.

76
06:23.000 --> 06:26.667
[Mercedes] Could you ask him to call me? Will you jot down my number?

77
06:27.417 --> 06:29.917
[Belén] Listen, your dad is not okay.

78
06:30.625 --> 06:33.292
He isn't okay at all.

79
06:34.271 --> 06:35.749
[Mercedes] What do you mean?

80
06:35.833 --> 06:37.478
[Belén] He's dying, Mercedes.

81
06:38.167 --> 06:39.690
He doesn't have much time left.

82
06:39.774 --> 06:43.166
If you want to speak to him, you'd better come and see him.

83
06:43.250 --> 06:44.625
And soon.

84
06:50.735 --> 06:52.292
[pensive music continues]

85
07:08.000 --> 07:08.841
[Mercedes] Hello?

86
07:11.083 --> 07:13.000
[music fades out]

87
07:18.042 --> 07:18.883
Hello?

88
07:29.083 --> 07:30.083
[Belén] Mercedes?

89
07:32.625 --> 07:33.541
Belén?

90
07:33.625 --> 07:36.082
- Yes. - [Mercedes] Nice to meet you.

91
07:37.073 --> 07:40.541
- Sorry I let myself in, I just… - [Belén] No, it's fine.

92
07:40.625 --> 07:41.466
Welcome.

93
07:43.042 --> 07:44.541
So we finally meet, huh?

94
07:44.625 --> 07:47.208
After so long…

95
07:48.083 --> 07:50.874
- I wasn't sure you'd come. - Yeah, me neither.

96
07:50.958 --> 07:51.874
Um…

97
07:51.958 --> 07:54.542
- Was it hard to find-- - Can I see Jaime?

98
07:55.875 --> 07:57.499
Yeah, of course.

99
07:57.583 --> 07:58.541
Follow me.

100
08:10.083 --> 08:11.709
I'll see if he's awake.

101
08:11.793 --> 08:13.541
[ominous music resumes]

102
08:17.498 --> 08:18.614
[Belén] Jaime.

103
08:20.333 --> 08:21.833
You've got a visitor.

104
08:22.583 --> 08:23.583
Should I let her in?

105
08:26.958 --> 08:27.875
You can come in.

106
08:34.567 --> 08:37.144
[ominous music continues]

107
08:44.542 --> 08:45.417
Hello, Jaime.

108
08:46.625 --> 08:47.542
How are you?

109
09:08.292 --> 09:09.133
Jaime.

110
09:10.417 --> 09:11.258
Do you hear me?

111
09:18.875 --> 09:19.792
Look, Dad.

112
09:20.667 --> 09:22.459
Look who's come to visit us.

113
09:23.208 --> 09:24.292
[weakly] Huh?

114
09:25.282 --> 09:26.123
Who is it?

115
09:26.917 --> 09:27.875
Your daughter.

116
09:28.500 --> 09:30.750
Mercedes. You do remember her, don't you?

117
09:32.667 --> 09:33.750
Is she here?

118
09:34.583 --> 09:35.458
Hello, Jaime.

119
09:40.375 --> 09:41.792
At last…

120
09:44.542 --> 09:47.208
- You came back. - [whispering] Yeah.

121
09:47.292 --> 09:49.584
- [Jaime] It's been so long. - I'm here.

122
09:54.125 --> 09:56.958
They told me you'd never come back,

123
09:57.583 --> 09:59.791
and that you were dead.

124
09:59.875 --> 10:01.125
What?

125
10:02.958 --> 10:06.458
[Jaime chuckles] Julián? Dead? Not a chance.

126
10:07.000 --> 10:08.708
I didn't believe them.

127
10:09.792 --> 10:12.000
They said I was crazy.

128
10:12.875 --> 10:15.624
I knew you wouldn't abandon me.

129
10:15.708 --> 10:17.916
Come, give me a hug.

130
10:18.000 --> 10:21.166
Look, Jaime. I'm your daughter, Mercedes.

131
10:21.250 --> 10:22.417
My brother is dead.

132
10:23.083 --> 10:24.499
What's wrong, son?

133
10:24.583 --> 10:27.250
- Julián, are you okay? - [Mercedes] Okay.

134
10:27.917 --> 10:29.124
It's okay, Dad.

135
10:29.208 --> 10:32.916
- You can keep talking later. Okay. - [Jaime] Julián, are you okay?

136
10:33.000 --> 10:35.709
Time for your meds, Dad. Here.

137
10:35.793 --> 10:36.708
[Belén] Dad.

138
10:36.792 --> 10:38.416
Open your mouth.

139
10:40.741 --> 10:41.582
There you go.

140
10:42.779 --> 10:43.620
Water.

141
10:44.583 --> 10:47.291
- Water. - [Jaime sips]

142
10:47.375 --> 10:49.458
Very good. Okay.

143
10:52.792 --> 10:54.217
[pillbox closes]

144
10:55.250 --> 10:57.166
[Mercedes] What does he have, exactly?

145
10:57.250 --> 11:00.250
He suffers from irreversible neurological deterioration.

146
11:02.042 --> 11:03.576
It was mild at first,

147
11:03.660 --> 11:06.584
but it's got worse over the last few months.

148
11:07.333 --> 11:09.458
He wouldn't eat nor get out of bed.

149
11:09.542 --> 11:11.040
But he's lucid.

150
11:11.124 --> 11:13.416
Not so much as before.

151
11:13.500 --> 11:14.874
He recognizes you.

152
11:14.958 --> 11:16.791
That's not always the case.

153
11:17.292 --> 11:18.916
Has he been examined by a doctor?

154
11:19.000 --> 11:21.333
- Yes, several of them. - What did they say?

155
11:21.417 --> 11:23.999
[Belén] The main problem is his heart.

156
11:24.083 --> 11:25.166
It's very weak.

157
11:25.250 --> 11:26.916
I'm not gonna lie to you.

158
11:27.000 --> 11:29.208
I think it's a matter of days now.

159
11:30.458 --> 11:32.083
He's letting himself die.

160
11:35.208 --> 11:36.125
I don't get it.

161
11:37.248 --> 11:40.291
I don't get how he wrote that letter in such a state.

162
11:40.375 --> 11:42.165
- It makes no sense. - What letter?

163
11:42.249 --> 11:44.583
The one he sent to the publishing house.

164
11:44.667 --> 11:46.583
I don't know what you're talking about.

165
11:46.667 --> 11:48.292
It's a letter.

166
12:00.250 --> 12:01.625
I had no clue about this.

167
12:02.875 --> 12:05.083
Someone must've helped him 'cause--

168
12:05.167 --> 12:06.666
There's only me here.

169
12:06.750 --> 12:08.917
Then how would you explain this?

170
12:10.792 --> 12:12.458
Maybe he wrote it some time ago,

171
12:12.542 --> 12:14.416
when he was still fine.

172
12:14.500 --> 12:17.041
No, the date is recent. Look--

173
12:17.125 --> 12:18.559
I don't know what to tell you.

174
12:23.750 --> 12:24.591
Okay.

175
12:30.122 --> 12:31.749
- You're leaving? - [Mercedes] I am.

176
12:31.833 --> 12:34.749
I'll look around for a place to crash

177
12:34.833 --> 12:36.958
and be back tomorrow to try and talk to him.

178
12:40.208 --> 12:41.108
Thank you, Belén.

179
12:42.708 --> 12:43.708
[Belén] Well…

180
12:45.292 --> 12:47.364
you can stay here if you want.

181
12:47.875 --> 12:49.042
There's plenty of room.

182
12:49.625 --> 12:52.791
Oh no, I don't want to cause you any more trouble.

183
12:52.875 --> 12:55.042
Oh, not at all. I'd be pleased.

184
12:55.625 --> 12:56.466
Besides,

185
12:57.042 --> 12:59.374
this is your house.

186
12:59.458 --> 13:00.299
Okay.

187
13:01.574 --> 13:02.415
[Belén chuckles]

188
13:04.292 --> 13:05.374
[chuckles softly]

189
13:05.458 --> 13:08.166
I was literally dying to know you.

190
13:08.708 --> 13:11.708
[suspenseful music]

191
13:14.833 --> 13:16.666
You can leave your stuff here.

192
13:23.667 --> 13:25.628
My room's next door, so…

193
13:26.542 --> 13:27.625
we'll be close.

194
13:30.467 --> 13:33.095
[suspenseful music continues]

195
13:37.000 --> 13:39.667
- I can give you another room. - No, it's fine.

196
13:42.654 --> 13:44.637
Your dad never wanted to change anything.

197
13:45.865 --> 13:47.292
He left everything untouched.

198
13:53.667 --> 13:56.084
- Do you need anything? - I just want to rest.

199
13:58.171 --> 13:59.091
[whispering] Okay.

200
14:10.052 --> 14:11.978
[suspenseful music intensifies]

201
14:46.606 --> 14:48.061
[sets the frame on the table]

202
15:17.333 --> 15:18.708
[music fades out]

203
15:19.500 --> 15:21.667
There are bedsheets,

204
15:22.375 --> 15:23.541
towels…

205
15:23.625 --> 15:24.613
[Mercedes] Mm-hmm.

206
15:25.125 --> 15:27.000
Do you have any sleepwear?

207
15:27.750 --> 15:29.124
Mmm. No, it's okay.

208
15:29.208 --> 15:33.083
I was planning on staying somewhere near to work,

209
15:33.167 --> 15:34.209
so it's cool.

210
15:35.792 --> 15:37.041
So…

211
15:37.125 --> 15:38.500
do you have anything new?

212
15:39.991 --> 15:40.832
New?

213
15:41.500 --> 15:44.000
A novel, something to share…

214
15:45.000 --> 15:46.124
[Mercedes] Mmm.

215
15:46.208 --> 15:47.050
Not for now.

216
15:47.134 --> 15:49.333
I mean, I should, but…

217
15:49.917 --> 15:52.167
What? You're dealing with a creative block?

218
15:52.833 --> 15:53.674
Yeah, kind of.

219
15:55.333 --> 15:59.000
Well, maybe you'll find some inspiration around here.

220
16:01.000 --> 16:04.792
[ominous music]

221
16:12.042 --> 16:13.722
[ominous music continues]

222
16:19.167 --> 16:20.708
[Belén] Here, Dad.

223
16:20.792 --> 16:21.791
[cutlery clinking]

224
16:21.875 --> 16:23.140
[Belén] A bit more.

225
16:25.958 --> 16:27.041
Mmm.

226
16:28.458 --> 16:29.500
Very good, Dad.

227
16:32.917 --> 16:33.834
Right.

228
16:37.042 --> 16:39.084
Okay. Very good, Daddy.

229
16:41.000 --> 16:41.841
Mmm.

230
16:44.167 --> 16:47.624
Why didn't you tell me anything?

231
16:47.708 --> 16:49.375
[Jaime babbles]

232
16:50.625 --> 16:52.458
[Belén] I didn't know she'd come.

233
16:54.125 --> 16:54.966
It's okay.

234
16:56.083 --> 16:57.208
I'm gonna help you.

235
16:57.292 --> 17:00.086
- You know you can count on me. - [Jaime breathes heavily]

236
17:00.170 --> 17:01.850
[ominous music continues]

237
17:09.144 --> 17:10.394
[music fades out]

238
17:23.620 --> 17:24.542
[moans]

239
17:52.833 --> 17:54.625
[sighs]

240
17:55.875 --> 17:58.000
[ominous music]

241
17:59.564 --> 18:02.191
[exhales deeply]

242
18:10.917 --> 18:13.042
[music builds up]

243
18:20.875 --> 18:22.542
[music subsides]

244
18:29.951 --> 18:32.657
[scraping]

245
18:32.741 --> 18:34.888
[ominous music intensifies]

246
18:42.125 --> 18:43.593
[scraping]

247
18:43.677 --> 18:44.539
[growl]

248
18:47.000 --> 18:50.429
[sipping]

249
18:56.201 --> 18:57.323
[creaking]

250
19:08.208 --> 19:09.106
[frantic chirp]

251
19:11.917 --> 19:13.986
[skittering]

252
19:16.417 --> 19:19.459
[sipping]

253
19:26.830 --> 19:28.455
[sipping continues]

254
19:43.417 --> 19:44.259
Belén?

255
19:53.583 --> 19:56.416
[sipping continues]

256
20:02.083 --> 20:04.083
[music builds up]

257
20:11.083 --> 20:12.208
[dramatic sting]

258
20:13.042 --> 20:15.666
- I didn't mean to scare you. - What are you doing here?

259
20:15.750 --> 20:17.458
[Belén] You called me, didn't you?

260
20:18.792 --> 20:20.250
Are you okay? What's wrong?

261
20:21.333 --> 20:23.374
- There's blood. - Blood?

262
20:23.458 --> 20:24.583
The pillow, it…

263
20:30.460 --> 20:32.544
- [Belén] There's nothing here. - But I…

264
20:32.628 --> 20:34.083
[sipping]

265
20:34.167 --> 20:36.375
- Hey, what's wrong? - That sound.

266
20:38.000 --> 20:38.917
The sipping.

267
20:40.417 --> 20:41.333
You hear it?

268
20:41.417 --> 20:42.874
- Easy. - You hear it?

269
20:42.958 --> 20:44.833
Calm down, everything's fine.

270
20:45.708 --> 20:47.541
Everything's fine, okay?

271
20:47.625 --> 20:48.958
[sipping continues]

272
20:50.542 --> 20:52.375
You need to get some rest.

273
20:53.917 --> 20:54.875
Relax.

274
20:56.542 --> 20:58.542
It's been a tough one today.

275
21:01.917 --> 21:03.000
But you're here now.

276
21:04.542 --> 21:05.459
You're home.

277
21:07.833 --> 21:09.208
I'm gonna take care of you.

278
21:10.845 --> 21:12.542
I'm gonna take care of you forever.

279
21:12.626 --> 21:14.041
[ominous music continues]

280
21:31.083 --> 21:33.250
[sipping continues]

281
21:34.542 --> 21:36.916
[Mercedes gasps]

282
21:41.750 --> 21:42.668
[gasps]

283
21:42.752 --> 21:44.305
[music fades out]

284
21:47.167 --> 21:49.041
[knock on door]

285
21:49.125 --> 21:50.500
[Belén] Mercedes?

286
21:50.584 --> 21:51.541
[knock on door]

287
21:52.083 --> 21:53.208
Mercedes, are you okay?

288
21:53.292 --> 21:54.959
[door opens]

289
21:56.792 --> 21:58.333
I'm sorry, I heard noises.

290
21:58.417 --> 21:59.258
[Mercedes] Huh?

291
22:00.125 --> 22:01.750
Hey, what's wrong?

292
22:04.583 --> 22:07.916
I just had a nightmare and I…

293
22:09.292 --> 22:11.541
- [Belén] Okay. - I got hurt, I don't know.

294
22:11.625 --> 22:13.708
Maybe you bite yourself while sleeping.

295
22:14.438 --> 22:15.875
It happens to me all the time.

296
22:17.167 --> 22:18.008
Come.

297
22:21.083 --> 22:21.924
Okay.

298
22:22.708 --> 22:23.549
It's fine.

299
22:25.875 --> 22:27.542
Call me if you need anything, okay?

300
22:29.000 --> 22:29.886
[whispering] Yeah.

301
22:30.750 --> 22:31.667
Good night.

302
22:35.958 --> 22:36.916
Good night.

303
22:44.125 --> 22:47.417
[ominous music]

304
22:57.833 --> 22:58.833
Morning, Jaime.

305
23:02.542 --> 23:03.667
You feel better today?

306
23:04.540 --> 23:06.042
Did you get some rest?

307
23:07.250 --> 23:08.708
Where's Belén?

308
23:09.542 --> 23:11.086
- She's there. - [Jaime] Belén!

309
23:11.170 --> 23:13.041
I'm right here, Daddy.

310
23:13.125 --> 23:14.496
I'm right here with you.

311
23:14.580 --> 23:15.583
Calm down.

312
23:16.208 --> 23:17.049
Jaime,

313
23:17.875 --> 23:20.708
you wrote me this letter asking me to come visit you.

314
23:27.833 --> 23:28.674
No…

315
23:29.417 --> 23:31.333
I didn't write this.

316
23:31.417 --> 23:34.499
[Mercedes] Okay. Do you remember who helped you writing it?

317
23:34.583 --> 23:36.697
How did you get to the post office?

318
23:36.781 --> 23:38.082
Did someone take you there?

319
23:38.166 --> 23:40.416
[muttering] That bitch.

320
23:40.546 --> 23:42.491
[flies buzzing]

321
23:42.625 --> 23:45.083
That dirty bitch!

322
23:45.167 --> 23:46.625
Don't scratch yourself.

323
23:47.375 --> 23:50.166
- Don't scratch yourself. - [Jaime] Nasty bitch.

324
23:50.250 --> 23:52.291
[Belén] Not again, Dad. Please.

325
23:52.375 --> 23:54.916
- [ominous music continues] - That dirty bitch!

326
23:55.000 --> 23:58.374
Dirty bitch!

327
23:58.458 --> 23:59.916
That dirty little…

328
24:00.000 --> 24:03.456
Dirty little fucker!

329
24:03.540 --> 24:06.084
[cries uncontrollably]

330
24:06.751 --> 24:11.208
Dirty little bitch!

331
24:12.083 --> 24:16.208
[mumbling] That dirty… dirty little…

332
24:17.880 --> 24:20.624
[whimpers]

333
24:20.708 --> 24:23.249
- [Belén] Easy, Dad. - What did you inject him with?

334
24:23.333 --> 24:24.583
Morphine.

335
24:25.292 --> 24:27.496
It helps him overcome crises.

336
24:27.580 --> 24:28.827
[ominous music fades out]

337
24:28.911 --> 24:30.271
And those marks?

338
24:31.120 --> 24:32.167
They're bedsores.

339
24:33.333 --> 24:35.208
He just spends a lot of time in bed.

340
24:36.500 --> 24:39.042
He scratches them and they get infected.

341
24:40.417 --> 24:42.334
Okay. It's okay now.

342
24:46.167 --> 24:47.542
Where are the horses?

343
24:48.277 --> 24:50.522
They were the only thing that made me come back.

344
24:51.250 --> 24:52.583
[Belén] They're gone.

345
24:54.229 --> 24:55.745
Did you use to come here a lot?

346
24:58.750 --> 25:00.413
We just spent one summer here.

347
25:01.583 --> 25:03.208
I think I was ten.

348
25:04.750 --> 25:07.833
After that, my parents separated

349
25:08.997 --> 25:10.084
and I never came back.

350
25:11.875 --> 25:14.167
That's when you guys stopped seeing each other?

351
25:16.208 --> 25:17.125
"Guys…"

352
25:18.500 --> 25:19.341
I mean,

353
25:20.292 --> 25:21.459
if you can call it that.

354
25:24.414 --> 25:26.292
Do you still hold a grudge against him?

355
25:31.917 --> 25:34.043
Some things are not easily forgiven, Belén.

356
25:34.127 --> 25:38.875
[distant thunder]

357
25:47.125 --> 25:48.283
[Mercedes] And your dad?

358
25:50.000 --> 25:50.875
He never existed.

359
25:53.417 --> 25:55.777
Jaime is the closest thing to a father I ever had.

360
25:58.042 --> 25:59.584
Now with Mom gone,

361
26:00.375 --> 26:02.042
he's the only family I have left.

362
26:04.042 --> 26:05.959
And you too, in a way.

363
26:08.625 --> 26:11.895
Have you decided what you'll do with the farm when Jaime's gone?

364
26:14.583 --> 26:15.458
No, I haven't.

365
26:18.208 --> 26:19.049
[Belén] Well, I…

366
26:19.848 --> 26:22.250
I've got some ideas for this place.

367
26:23.417 --> 26:25.209
Maybe we could partner up.

368
26:26.542 --> 26:28.147
I could stay and live here

369
26:28.231 --> 26:30.625
and you could come every so often to write.

370
26:32.000 --> 26:34.083
We could make it work.

371
26:36.125 --> 26:36.966
Maybe.

372
26:40.954 --> 26:41.795
[Belén] Jesús!

373
26:46.333 --> 26:48.749
- Morning. How are you? - [Jesús] Morning.

374
26:48.833 --> 26:51.166
[Belén] This is Mercedes. She's Jaime's daughter.

375
26:51.250 --> 26:53.125
- Nice to meet you. - Same.

376
26:53.896 --> 26:55.446
Jaime's daughter, huh?

377
26:55.958 --> 26:58.458
His real daughter. I'm more like an impostor.

378
26:58.542 --> 26:59.584
Don't say that.

379
27:00.292 --> 27:01.927
[Belén] Jesús works at the farm.

380
27:02.011 --> 27:04.042
He makes it all work. Don't you?

381
27:04.917 --> 27:06.087
Like your father said--

382
27:06.171 --> 27:08.416
Like your father says,

383
27:09.042 --> 27:11.398
"Jesús is our savior."

384
27:12.036 --> 27:15.206
- These are the week's groceries. - [Belén] Okay.

385
27:15.290 --> 27:17.492
- Should I take them to the house? - I can do it.

386
27:17.576 --> 27:19.374
- You sure? - Yeah. Would you help me?

387
27:19.458 --> 27:20.344
Of course.

388
27:20.428 --> 27:22.553
See, Jesús? We don't need you.

389
27:23.708 --> 27:25.041
- Here you go. - Okay, then.

390
27:26.375 --> 27:28.625
- I'll be right here if you need me. - Thanks.

391
27:30.792 --> 27:34.250
[ominous music]

392
27:40.250 --> 27:42.100
[music builds up]

393
28:00.708 --> 28:01.959
[music fades out]

394
28:31.083 --> 28:33.792
- Is everything okay? - [Mercedes] Yeah, I was just…

395
28:35.000 --> 28:37.583
Actually, I'd like to stay here a few days more.

396
28:38.875 --> 28:40.125
I really want to…

397
28:40.913 --> 28:42.416
talk to him before--

398
28:42.500 --> 28:43.341
I get it.

399
28:44.613 --> 28:46.416
[Mercedes] I mean, if you don't mind.

400
28:46.500 --> 28:48.583
Oh no. Not at all.

401
28:50.625 --> 28:52.643
We could take care of him together.

402
28:53.125 --> 28:54.333
I could teach you how.

403
28:56.583 --> 28:57.424
Yeah.

404
28:58.446 --> 29:01.000
There's one other thing I wanted to talk to you about.

405
29:02.417 --> 29:04.209
I mean, it's just that…

406
29:05.205 --> 29:07.667
don't you think Jaime would be better off in a place

407
29:08.750 --> 29:10.916
where he's provided with medical care?

408
29:11.000 --> 29:11.958
What place?

409
29:12.042 --> 29:14.376
I don't know, a clinic or hospital.

410
29:14.460 --> 29:15.301
I don't think so.

411
29:16.333 --> 29:19.246
Listen, Belén, I'm not a doctor, but--

412
29:19.330 --> 29:20.171
Right.

413
29:21.000 --> 29:22.250
You're not.

414
29:23.000 --> 29:24.999
I know. All I say is that--

415
29:25.083 --> 29:28.333
Look, I'm just trying to respect his will.

416
29:29.250 --> 29:31.041
I may not be his biological daughter,

417
29:31.125 --> 29:33.583
but I know he doesn't want to die in a hospital,

418
29:34.375 --> 29:35.917
but here, at home.

419
29:39.500 --> 29:40.746
Do you want to stay?

420
29:40.830 --> 29:42.705
You can stay as long as you want.

421
29:44.330 --> 29:47.958
But you haven't seen him in 25 years.

422
29:50.542 --> 29:53.626
So please don't tell me how to handle things.

423
29:53.710 --> 29:56.500
[tense music]

424
30:25.879 --> 30:27.484
[tense music builds up]

425
30:27.639 --> 30:29.417
MY BROTHER'S BODY…

426
30:33.958 --> 30:36.500
WAS STILL SWINGING WHEN I GOT TO THE SHED.

427
31:45.500 --> 31:46.814
[music fades out]

428
31:53.958 --> 31:54.799
It's ready.

429
31:57.833 --> 31:58.674
[Jesús] Mmm.

430
32:03.750 --> 32:04.958
[Mercedes] Okay.

431
32:07.792 --> 32:10.333
- You really don't want to eat? - [Belén] I'm okay.

432
32:10.417 --> 32:13.042
Oh, come on. Don't be disrespectful to our cook.

433
32:14.208 --> 32:15.333
I'm sorry, I can't.

434
32:15.417 --> 32:17.746
I'm on a detox

435
32:17.830 --> 32:20.038
and I can just have this.

436
32:24.458 --> 32:25.333
[Jesús] Beer?

437
32:26.292 --> 32:27.296
No, thanks.

438
32:27.380 --> 32:29.917
- You? - [Mercedes] Yes, please. A toast?

439
32:31.581 --> 32:32.916
- Come on. - I really can't.

440
32:33.000 --> 32:35.167
- Please. - [Jesús] Oh, don't be like that.

441
32:35.750 --> 32:38.125
Okay. Just because it's you.

442
32:38.792 --> 32:40.292
- [Mercedes] Cheers. - Cheers.

443
32:49.125 --> 32:49.966
Mmm!

444
32:50.750 --> 32:51.999
This is so good.

445
32:52.083 --> 32:54.458
- You're missing on it. - Mmm.

446
32:54.542 --> 32:58.042
Okay, stop. I'm really making a sacrifice here.

447
33:00.375 --> 33:03.208
So you're on a yogurt diet?

448
33:04.292 --> 33:05.250
No, it's not yogurt.

449
33:06.083 --> 33:07.875
It's a typical brew from the area.

450
33:09.250 --> 33:10.666
They make it in town.

451
33:10.750 --> 33:13.874
It helps you cleanse your mind and body.

452
33:13.958 --> 33:16.791
Women have it when they wanna get pregnant.

453
33:16.875 --> 33:18.388
They say chances are higher.

454
33:18.917 --> 33:21.117
- You wanna get pregnant? - [Belén] No, I don't.

455
33:21.201 --> 33:22.291
[chuckles]

456
33:22.375 --> 33:23.216
Okay.

457
33:23.833 --> 33:24.875
Do you want some?

458
33:26.250 --> 33:27.708
Definitely not.

459
33:28.667 --> 33:30.167
You never wanted to be a mom?

460
33:31.583 --> 33:32.708
I'm not mom material.

461
33:33.625 --> 33:38.209
And even if I was, I don't have the time to devote to it.

462
33:38.718 --> 33:41.746
Besides, I'm at the peak of my career, so, uh-uh, no chance.

463
33:41.830 --> 33:43.872
[Jesús] Belén told me you're a writer.

464
33:44.500 --> 33:46.949
Can you honestly make a living off of writing books?

465
33:47.033 --> 33:49.000
You can if you sell enough of them.

466
33:49.974 --> 33:53.124
[Belén] Mercedes is one of the most famous authors of the country.

467
33:53.208 --> 33:54.916
No, I'm not. No.

468
33:55.000 --> 33:56.367
- Yes, you are. - I'm not.

469
33:56.451 --> 33:58.499
You should read her novels. You'd love them.

470
33:58.583 --> 34:00.916
Well, they're supposed to frighten you, so…

471
34:01.000 --> 34:03.387
- They're horror stories. - [Mercedes] Mmm-hmm.

472
34:03.471 --> 34:04.666
[Belén] Mmm-hmm.

473
34:04.750 --> 34:07.375
They all take place in this town, right?

474
34:08.542 --> 34:10.124
No, it's a fictional town,

475
34:10.208 --> 34:11.706
so it could be any town.

476
34:12.109 --> 34:13.516
But they're identical, right?

477
34:13.958 --> 34:16.391
I mean, the descriptions, the landscapes, the farm…

478
34:16.475 --> 34:17.668
Which novel did you read?

479
34:17.752 --> 34:19.048
All three of them.

480
34:19.875 --> 34:21.269
The ones that were published.

481
34:23.208 --> 34:25.541
And Jaime? Has he read any of them?

482
34:25.625 --> 34:29.625
I read them to him when he was still okay.

483
34:30.458 --> 34:31.299
So?

484
34:31.917 --> 34:32.917
Did he like them?

485
34:34.830 --> 34:36.008
He never told me.

486
34:38.417 --> 34:41.626
But… I know he's beyond proud of you.

487
34:41.710 --> 34:44.083
[ominous music]

488
34:48.875 --> 34:49.833
Okay, Jaime.

489
34:52.080 --> 34:53.792
Come on, Jaime.

490
35:01.750 --> 35:02.833
[sighs]

491
35:02.917 --> 35:04.334
You didn't eat a bite.

492
35:08.583 --> 35:12.291
All right, meds time.

493
35:14.354 --> 35:15.689
[whispering] Come on, Jaime.

494
35:32.875 --> 35:35.126
You really don't know who I am, do you?

495
35:35.210 --> 35:36.875
[breathes heavily]

496
35:38.375 --> 35:39.250
[Mercedes] Okay.

497
35:40.250 --> 35:41.375
[whispering] Rest up.

498
35:46.259 --> 35:47.292
Is it okay like this?

499
35:52.542 --> 35:53.459
[sighs]

500
35:57.333 --> 35:58.666
[music fades out]

501
36:02.875 --> 36:04.167
[Jaime] Get it off me.

502
36:04.958 --> 36:05.947
What did you say?

503
36:06.031 --> 36:09.500
Julián, son, get it off me.

504
36:10.375 --> 36:12.458
Are you hot? I can take off the blanket.

505
36:13.667 --> 36:15.292
[ominous music]

506
36:17.000 --> 36:21.000
[laboriously] The bug's killing me.

507
36:21.583 --> 36:23.625
- [Jaime] Get it off me. - What bug?

508
36:24.565 --> 36:26.956
What are you talking about? Don't scratch yourself.

509
36:27.040 --> 36:29.996
- Don't do that. You'll hurt yourself. - [Jaime cries]

510
36:30.080 --> 36:30.999
Jaime, don't.

511
36:31.083 --> 36:33.124
- [grunts] - [Mercedes] Jaime! Jaime, don't!

512
36:33.208 --> 36:34.583
- [cries] - [Mercedes] Don't!

513
36:35.710 --> 36:38.249
[crying]

514
36:38.333 --> 36:39.708
Get it off me!

515
36:39.792 --> 36:40.958
[shrieks]

516
36:41.042 --> 36:42.796
[music continues]

517
36:42.880 --> 36:43.999
[Mercedes] Belén!

518
36:44.083 --> 36:47.792
- [Jaime] Please help me! - [Mercedes] Belén!

519
36:48.375 --> 36:49.999
- Help me! - Okay, okay.

520
36:50.083 --> 36:52.768
- Please get it off me! - Okay, Jaime. Okay.

521
36:53.238 --> 36:54.993
- [Jaime] Get it off me! - Okay.

522
36:56.040 --> 36:57.586
Help me!

523
36:57.670 --> 37:00.375
- Okay! Jaime… - [Jaime] Get it off me!

524
37:01.167 --> 37:02.750
Help me!

525
37:03.290 --> 37:05.291
[Jaime shrieks] No!

526
37:05.375 --> 37:06.216
It's okay.

527
37:07.269 --> 37:08.194
[screaming ceases]

528
37:11.260 --> 37:12.575
[music fades out]

529
37:12.670 --> 37:14.750
[wheezes]

530
37:22.042 --> 37:23.317
How is he?

531
37:23.875 --> 37:24.716
Better.

532
37:32.000 --> 37:33.208
Did you follow the dose?

533
37:34.125 --> 37:36.679
Yes, just like you told me this morning.

534
37:38.250 --> 37:39.091
Are you sure?

535
37:40.292 --> 37:41.133
[Mercedes] Yes.

536
37:46.784 --> 37:47.625
Belén.

537
37:49.667 --> 37:51.292
Something's off with his belly.

538
37:53.917 --> 37:55.625
Something kind of moved…

539
37:56.958 --> 37:57.799
inside it.

540
37:59.125 --> 38:00.083
Something like what?

541
38:02.708 --> 38:04.841
I-I don't know what it was,

542
38:04.925 --> 38:06.499
but there's something inside him.

543
38:06.583 --> 38:07.666
Something weird…

544
38:08.333 --> 38:10.208
- [tense music] - Mmm?

545
38:10.292 --> 38:11.375
- [Mercedes] He-- - Hey.

546
38:12.375 --> 38:14.208
Easy. He'll be fine.

547
38:14.292 --> 38:15.416
Don't worry.

548
38:15.500 --> 38:18.291
You didn't heard what I said. There's something inside him.

549
38:19.167 --> 38:20.084
I did hear you.

550
38:21.583 --> 38:22.424
But look at him.

551
38:23.922 --> 38:25.375
[Belén] There's nothing there.

552
38:28.792 --> 38:32.666
Look. We can call the doctor tomorrow to examine him

553
38:32.750 --> 38:35.125
and make sure he's all right, mmm?

554
38:35.667 --> 38:36.508
Okay?

555
38:40.500 --> 38:41.341
Okay.

556
38:44.818 --> 38:49.343
[tense music continues]

557
39:03.000 --> 39:04.661
[doctor] I'll adjust some doses.

558
39:06.292 --> 39:07.667
I detailed them here.

559
39:09.583 --> 39:11.166
If he doesn't eat or move,

560
39:12.167 --> 39:14.273
you need to come to terms with the idea that…

561
39:14.958 --> 39:16.197
[Belén] Thank you, doctor.

562
39:18.000 --> 39:19.500
[doctor] In case you need it.

563
39:23.083 --> 39:23.924
Morphine?

564
39:25.375 --> 39:27.750
This final stage is the most difficult.

565
39:28.421 --> 39:30.627
- We don't want him to suffer further. - Exactly.

566
39:30.711 --> 39:33.958
Don't you think Jaime would be better off at a hospital?

567
39:34.042 --> 39:36.336
I could cover the expenses.

568
39:36.420 --> 39:38.666
Did he try to escape again?

569
39:38.750 --> 39:40.125
- No. - [tense music]

570
39:41.170 --> 39:44.751
Whether at home or at hospital, his condition won't improve.

571
39:45.501 --> 39:47.091
[doctor] It's up to you to decide

572
39:47.175 --> 39:49.666
how and where he'll spend his final moments.

573
39:49.750 --> 39:53.092
If you can afford it and take care of him the way you've been doing it,

574
39:53.833 --> 39:55.708
my advice is you let him stay here.

575
39:57.750 --> 39:58.901
Now if you'll excuse me…

576
39:59.875 --> 40:00.716
It's okay.

577
40:10.208 --> 40:11.874
- You're okay now? - [Mercedes] No.

578
40:11.958 --> 40:13.333
No, I'm not okay.

579
40:14.330 --> 40:16.458
What did he mean he tried to escape, Belén?

580
40:17.051 --> 40:18.996
Never mind, it happened long ago.

581
40:19.080 --> 40:21.144
We found him on the way to town.

582
40:21.228 --> 40:22.206
When did it happen?

583
40:22.290 --> 40:24.956
- A few weeks ago. - [Mercedes] A few weeks?

584
40:25.040 --> 40:26.666
When were you planning to tell me?

585
40:26.750 --> 40:30.099
Hasn't it occurred to you that maybe that's when he sent me the letter?

586
40:30.183 --> 40:33.593
I don't care what the doctor says, this isn't the best place for Jaime,

587
40:33.677 --> 40:34.999
let alone in his state.

588
40:35.083 --> 40:36.496
- Again? - What?

589
40:36.580 --> 40:39.536
This house is isolated and you're here on your own.

590
40:39.620 --> 40:41.666
So far I've managed quite well.

591
40:41.750 --> 40:44.876
You have? 'Cause you didn't hear me when I called you yesterday.

592
40:44.960 --> 40:48.166
- Yesterday, for the first time in months… - [Mercedes] Yeah?

593
40:48.250 --> 40:49.958
…I relaxed for a moment

594
40:50.042 --> 40:52.336
'cause I thought you'd cover for me.

595
40:52.420 --> 40:56.166
- But you didn't even last five minutes. - He almost died within those five--

596
40:56.250 --> 40:57.176
If you're implying

597
40:57.260 --> 41:00.565
I'm not taking care of him as I should and that I'm not suitable for--

598
41:00.649 --> 41:01.746
I'm not implying that!

599
41:01.830 --> 41:05.746
I just think Jaime needs professional care and you need to rest.

600
41:05.830 --> 41:08.208
What my dad needs is to die in peace.

601
41:08.917 --> 41:11.296
And what I need is none of your business.

602
41:11.380 --> 41:14.717
That's how it's always been, and will continue to be once you're gone.

603
41:22.875 --> 41:24.888
[tense music continues]

604
41:26.084 --> 41:27.455
FRESH MILK

605
41:49.417 --> 41:51.542
[suspenseful music]

606
42:20.137 --> 42:22.624
Sorry, I poured myself some. I just wanted to try it.

607
42:22.708 --> 42:24.291
- [Belén] It's okay. - Really?

608
42:26.875 --> 42:27.833
Are you okay?

609
42:28.792 --> 42:29.959
Yeah, I'm fine.

610
42:33.833 --> 42:35.416
Belén, can I help you?

611
42:35.500 --> 42:37.500
- You're-- - [Belén] I'm okay. [burps]

612
42:38.042 --> 42:39.042
[breathes heavily]

613
42:43.000 --> 42:45.374
[retches]

614
42:45.458 --> 42:46.666
Belén?

615
42:46.750 --> 42:48.234
[suspenseful music continues]

616
42:49.042 --> 42:49.916
[burps]

617
42:50.000 --> 42:51.583
[retches]

618
42:51.667 --> 42:53.459
What's wrong? Belén?

619
42:54.290 --> 42:55.666
[Belén] Leave me alone.

620
42:56.514 --> 42:57.500
[gasps, retches]

621
43:06.905 --> 43:08.651
[retches]

622
43:21.750 --> 43:22.667
[Mercedes] Belén.

623
43:27.583 --> 43:28.750
[door closes]

624
43:42.625 --> 43:44.083
[music fades out]

625
43:44.833 --> 43:48.291
[Belén cries]

626
43:58.077 --> 43:59.036
Belén?

627
43:59.120 --> 44:01.458
[Belén continues crying]

628
44:02.167 --> 44:03.125
[knocks on door]

629
44:04.333 --> 44:05.749
Belén, are you all right?

630
44:05.833 --> 44:07.958
[Belén] Just leave me alone!

631
44:09.000 --> 44:11.552
- [brooding dramatic music] - [Belén continues crying]

632
44:23.306 --> 44:24.614
[Belén continues crying]

633
44:26.042 --> 44:28.417
[electrical crackling]

634
44:35.083 --> 44:37.661
[crackling continues]

635
44:38.737 --> 44:39.587
[crying ceases]

636
44:57.500 --> 44:59.500
[brooding dramatic music continues]

637
45:11.250 --> 45:12.791
[music fades out]

638
45:12.875 --> 45:14.374
[types]

639
45:14.458 --> 45:17.709
[Mercedes] The bug was already there when my father bought the house.

640
45:19.875 --> 45:21.833
The house where we spent that summer.

641
45:22.833 --> 45:25.000
At least, that's what my brother said,

642
45:25.583 --> 45:28.291
that a monstrous insect visited him every night

643
45:28.958 --> 45:31.083
and was slowly driving him mad.

644
45:48.000 --> 45:49.633
[types]

645
45:49.717 --> 45:52.000
Nobody believed him when he showed us the marks.

646
45:53.417 --> 45:55.624
My parents said he gave them to himself,

647
45:57.167 --> 45:58.584
that Julián was sick,

648
45:59.500 --> 46:00.708
sick to the head.

649
46:01.875 --> 46:03.590
That's how they explained it to me.

650
46:04.792 --> 46:06.875
No one ever mentioned that night again.

651
46:08.042 --> 46:11.125
The night that I accepted to be on guard at the foot of his bed,

652
46:12.375 --> 46:14.708
ready to shoot as soon as it showed up

653
46:14.792 --> 46:16.040
[continues typing]

654
46:16.208 --> 46:18.833
and determined to keep my promise of not falling asleep.

655
46:18.917 --> 46:19.874
[yawns]

656
46:22.292 --> 46:24.375
I don't know when sleep won the fight.

657
46:26.167 --> 46:28.084
But it was a sound, infinite sleep

658
46:29.542 --> 46:30.709
I'm still unsure

659
46:31.917 --> 46:33.776
I have woken up from.

660
46:46.250 --> 46:48.292
[snoring]

661
46:54.277 --> 46:56.248
[Jaime snores]

662
46:56.382 --> 46:58.103
[brooding dramatic music resumes]

663
47:11.500 --> 47:13.083
[dramatic sting]

664
47:14.574 --> 47:15.415
[music fades out]

665
47:16.625 --> 47:17.583
[Belén] Mercedes.

666
47:19.792 --> 47:21.000
[Mercedes] You called me?

667
47:22.458 --> 47:23.367
[Belén] Come on in.

668
47:25.417 --> 47:26.375
How are you feeling?

669
47:28.333 --> 47:31.166
[Belén sighs] I'm okay, but I'm exhausted.

670
47:31.644 --> 47:33.954
Mmm. Do you know what you got?

671
47:35.326 --> 47:37.515
[sighs] It was just my stomach. But I'm…

672
47:38.083 --> 47:38.999
[clears throat]

673
47:39.083 --> 47:41.436
I'm okay now. It happens to me sometimes.

674
47:42.250 --> 47:43.207
[Mercedes] Mmm-hmm.

675
47:44.114 --> 47:44.955
Come.

676
48:00.958 --> 48:02.041
You know…

677
48:03.583 --> 48:05.666
when my family split up, I just…

678
48:06.625 --> 48:08.583
I mean, my mom was a complicated woman

679
48:08.667 --> 48:11.709
and the relationship with my dad just… You know…

680
48:13.801 --> 48:15.374
I had my share of problems.

681
48:16.083 --> 48:17.952
I went through an eating disorder,

682
48:18.036 --> 48:20.374
- so I don't know if you-- - [electrical crackling]

683
48:20.458 --> 48:21.999
[suspenseful music]

684
48:22.083 --> 48:24.541
No, I don't think I have that.

685
48:27.089 --> 48:28.542
[Mercedes] Well, I think that…

686
48:29.125 --> 48:30.374
Hey, look.

687
48:30.458 --> 48:31.666
Look what I've got here.

688
48:31.750 --> 48:33.042
- [Mercedes] Oh? - Look.

689
48:37.917 --> 48:39.167
[music fades out]

690
48:41.625 --> 48:42.625
[Mercedes] Belén.

691
48:44.792 --> 48:47.250
- [Belén] See? I'm your biggest fan. - Mmm.

692
48:48.875 --> 48:51.438
So… do you want me to sign your copies for you?

693
48:52.083 --> 48:53.041
You'd better.

694
48:55.958 --> 48:56.799
Also…

695
48:58.250 --> 48:59.875
I didn't intend to…

696
49:00.917 --> 49:03.250
downplay what you've done for Jaime.

697
49:04.833 --> 49:06.416
Actually, I can only…

698
49:08.042 --> 49:09.209
thank you.

699
49:13.250 --> 49:14.875
I'm here if you need to talk.

700
49:16.625 --> 49:17.466
I know.

701
49:21.583 --> 49:22.750
Did you check on him?

702
49:23.880 --> 49:26.291
Yeah, he's… he's resting.

703
49:26.375 --> 49:28.249
I'll give him his dinner now.

704
49:28.333 --> 49:29.791
Would you rather I do it?

705
49:29.875 --> 49:31.086
[Mercedes] No, no, no.

706
49:31.170 --> 49:32.542
No, you get some rest.

707
49:34.954 --> 49:35.795
Here.

708
49:45.878 --> 49:49.003
[suspenseful music]

709
50:04.125 --> 50:04.966
Jaime?

710
50:15.083 --> 50:15.958
Jaime?

711
50:19.833 --> 50:20.674
[shouting] Belén!

712
50:22.167 --> 50:23.126
Belén!

713
50:23.210 --> 50:25.351
[suspenseful music continues]

714
50:56.208 --> 50:57.208
No, no, no, no, no.

715
50:58.500 --> 51:01.088
[music turns dramatic]

716
51:01.192 --> 51:02.916
No, no, no… No, no, no!

717
51:03.000 --> 51:04.458
No! Jaime, don't!

718
51:05.415 --> 51:07.132
No, no, no! Belén!

719
51:07.765 --> 51:08.640
Belén!

720
51:13.553 --> 51:14.811
[Belén] I'll do it. Wait.

721
51:16.330 --> 51:17.706
[Mercedes] Jaime! No, no!

722
51:17.790 --> 51:19.542
Please hurry. [gasps]

723
51:26.047 --> 51:27.583
[Mercedes pants]

724
51:27.667 --> 51:29.691
[music fades out]

725
51:31.417 --> 51:34.751
[Belén] We gotta keep a closer watch and be on permanent guard.

726
51:34.854 --> 51:37.086
I can stay with him tonight.

727
51:44.038 --> 51:44.879
[sighs]

728
51:45.667 --> 51:48.435
- I told you I don't drink. - Tonight will be an exception.

729
52:11.750 --> 52:13.246
I'd like to talk to you about--

730
52:13.330 --> 52:15.999
You'll tell me this wouldn't have happened at a hospital?

731
52:16.083 --> 52:16.996
No.

732
52:17.080 --> 52:18.070
So?

733
52:19.620 --> 52:22.168
Don't you think Jaime's trying to tell us something?

734
52:22.252 --> 52:23.996
What, exactly?

735
52:24.080 --> 52:26.499
It's quite obvious, Belén.

736
52:26.583 --> 52:27.458
Isn't it?

737
52:27.542 --> 52:28.908
What do you mean?

738
52:29.253 --> 52:30.959
We're not there, he kills himself.

739
52:32.333 --> 52:36.416
I mean, it doesn't make sense for him to keep suffering like this--

740
52:36.500 --> 52:37.749
I just don't get it.

741
52:37.833 --> 52:40.407
You wanna help him or take a weight off your shoulders?

742
52:40.491 --> 52:43.416
No, I just… Look, I'm saying exactly what the doctor said.

743
52:43.500 --> 52:46.133
- He suggested it. - We understood different things, then.

744
52:46.237 --> 52:49.750
- You said he's letting himself die. - That's his call to make, not mine.

745
52:50.375 --> 52:52.916
He's not some dog you can sacrifice.

746
52:53.000 --> 52:55.124
Who said anything about sacrificing him?

747
52:55.208 --> 52:57.791
All I say is we go and ask him what he really wants.

748
52:57.875 --> 52:59.708
Listen, just three days ago,

749
53:01.083 --> 53:04.221
your father was leading an orderly life along with a fixed routine

750
53:04.305 --> 53:05.996
and none of this had ever happened.

751
53:06.080 --> 53:07.734
Are you implying this is my fault?

752
53:08.756 --> 53:09.982
Well, maybe your presence

753
53:10.066 --> 53:12.282
doesn't exactly bring back the best memories.

754
53:14.282 --> 53:15.759
[Mercedes] Okay, mmm.

755
53:18.125 --> 53:18.966
You're right.

756
53:21.503 --> 53:24.416
Mmm, yeah. I guess it's better if I leave tomorrow

757
53:24.500 --> 53:25.875
'cause I…

758
53:27.042 --> 53:29.292
I'm not of much help here.

759
53:34.333 --> 53:36.916
[ominous music]

760
53:41.721 --> 53:43.865
[music continues]

761
53:56.375 --> 53:57.874
[sighs]

762
54:13.391 --> 54:15.709
[rustle]

763
54:21.204 --> 54:23.321
[insect scuttling]

764
54:44.298 --> 54:48.193
[music builds up]

765
54:49.945 --> 54:51.222
[music fades out]

766
54:51.306 --> 54:53.833
[sipping]

767
54:55.892 --> 54:57.633
[gasping]

768
55:02.120 --> 55:04.707
[sipping continues]

769
55:09.192 --> 55:11.600
[louder slurp]

770
55:18.167 --> 55:21.084
[suspenseful music]

771
55:47.417 --> 55:49.375
Belén doesn't serve my purpose.

772
55:52.917 --> 55:54.459
You're the one I need.

773
55:58.542 --> 56:00.459
[Jesús sips]

774
56:12.788 --> 56:13.706
[continues gasping]

775
56:13.790 --> 56:15.750
[music builds up]

776
56:21.960 --> 56:23.168
[Jesús stops sipping]

777
56:30.458 --> 56:31.416
[gasps]

778
56:37.330 --> 56:39.560
- [screams] - [music ends]

779
56:42.750 --> 56:45.208
[tense music]

780
57:02.375 --> 57:03.216
Belén?

781
57:14.960 --> 57:15.875
[whispering] Jaime?

782
57:19.936 --> 57:21.668
[Jaime breathes heavily]

783
57:26.250 --> 57:28.500
[mumbles]

784
57:29.858 --> 57:31.125
[dramatic sting]

785
57:32.920 --> 57:34.579
- [Belén] Are you okay? - No.

786
57:34.875 --> 57:37.376
I know what's going on. We must get out of here now.

787
57:37.460 --> 57:38.543
What are you saying?

788
57:39.625 --> 57:41.292
This may sound crazy,

789
57:42.625 --> 57:45.500
but there's a bug in this house, a parasite.

790
57:46.583 --> 57:48.875
- [Belén] You're delirious. - No. No, no, no.

791
57:49.792 --> 57:53.226
It comes at night and attacks us while we sleep. I swear, it's…

792
57:53.310 --> 57:54.541
Look.

793
57:54.625 --> 57:56.917
You must have this too. Why don't you…

794
57:57.501 --> 57:59.702
My brother always said something was off here,

795
58:00.583 --> 58:02.876
but no one believed him, not even me.

796
58:02.960 --> 58:05.208
And the same thing's happening to Jaime.

797
58:05.292 --> 58:06.624
He's not mad.

798
58:06.708 --> 58:08.916
- [Belén] Okay, breathe. - Belén, we… Oh, God.

799
58:09.542 --> 58:11.042
- [Belén] Breathe. - Okay.

800
58:12.083 --> 58:14.458
I think you're just imagining things.

801
58:14.542 --> 58:15.796
[Mercedes] I'm not crazy.

802
58:15.880 --> 58:18.541
- No, I didn't say you were. - [Mercedes] I…

803
58:18.625 --> 58:20.166
I'm just saying

804
58:20.250 --> 58:22.333
that everything you're going through

805
58:22.417 --> 58:24.956
is making you believe things that aren't true.

806
58:25.040 --> 58:26.958
Why don't you go and lie down?

807
58:27.042 --> 58:29.956
No. No, I'm… I'm not sleeping in that room.

808
58:30.040 --> 58:30.881
Come.

809
58:31.417 --> 58:32.624
Shh.

810
58:32.708 --> 58:33.751
[Mercedes sighs]

811
58:33.835 --> 58:36.458
[tense music continues]

812
58:42.250 --> 58:43.542
[Belén] Come here.

813
58:45.958 --> 58:48.666
- [Mercedes] No, I don't want-- - Just lie down.

814
58:48.750 --> 58:50.959
- I don't want to… - I'll take care of you.

815
58:51.833 --> 58:52.674
Okay?

816
58:53.250 --> 58:54.333
Now lie down.

817
58:54.417 --> 58:56.106
No. No, no, Belén.

818
58:56.625 --> 58:59.666
You really didn't hear or see anything strange in this house?

819
58:59.750 --> 59:01.667
Something like what? A bug?

820
59:02.750 --> 59:03.667
No.

821
59:04.667 --> 59:05.917
No, no, no.

822
59:06.875 --> 59:08.875
Well, this is the countryside, so bugs…

823
59:09.588 --> 59:10.791
are to be expected.

824
59:10.875 --> 59:12.417
That's completely normal.

825
59:14.500 --> 59:16.249
- Come on, lie down. - [Mercedes] No.

826
59:16.333 --> 59:18.727
Just lie down. I'll stay here with you for a while.

827
59:20.208 --> 59:21.291
Come on.

828
59:21.375 --> 59:22.216
[Mercedes] No…

829
59:23.167 --> 59:24.008
Hey.

830
59:25.458 --> 59:26.458
You're shaking.

831
59:29.042 --> 59:31.042
All right, let's do something.

832
59:31.792 --> 59:33.375
We'll talk to Jesús tomorrow

833
59:34.208 --> 59:36.541
and ask him to spray the house, okay?

834
59:37.417 --> 59:38.834
He knows about these things.

835
59:41.542 --> 59:42.833
All right?

836
59:42.917 --> 59:43.758
Okay.

837
59:44.540 --> 59:47.375
[suspenseful music]

838
01:00:03.871 --> 01:00:06.115
[music continues]

839
01:00:17.318 --> 01:00:19.996
[Mercedes] Um, Jesús? I think you should spray here too.

840
01:00:20.080 --> 01:00:20.951
The curtains are…

841
01:00:21.583 --> 01:00:24.541
There's not much to do in this room. I'm pretty much done here.

842
01:00:25.208 --> 01:00:28.246
But we still need to spray that area and the closet.

843
01:00:28.330 --> 01:00:30.375
I don't want to have my room sprayed

844
01:00:30.459 --> 01:00:32.333
'cause I have some fragile stuff there.

845
01:00:32.417 --> 01:00:33.376
How fragile?

846
01:00:33.460 --> 01:00:34.458
Fragile enough.

847
01:00:35.460 --> 01:00:37.458
[suspenseful music continues]

848
01:01:01.457 --> 01:01:02.964
[music fades out]

849
01:01:10.125 --> 01:01:11.333
So…

850
01:01:12.208 --> 01:01:13.208
you're leaving?

851
01:01:14.875 --> 01:01:16.223
It's for the best, isn't it?

852
01:01:17.458 --> 01:01:18.299
And Jaime?

853
01:01:19.750 --> 01:01:21.208
He'll be in very good hands.

854
01:01:35.167 --> 01:01:37.584
I've been thinking about it and…

855
01:01:39.458 --> 01:01:42.209
once Jaime's gone, I want you to keep the house.

856
01:01:43.292 --> 01:01:44.333
I'm serious.

857
01:01:44.417 --> 01:01:46.209
I think it's the right choice and…

858
01:01:47.702 --> 01:01:49.660
I know Jaime would want the same thing.

859
01:01:52.042 --> 01:01:53.806
I'll miss having you around.

860
01:02:09.040 --> 01:02:11.042
[ominous music]

861
01:02:12.208 --> 01:02:13.875
[electrical crackling]

862
01:02:18.960 --> 01:02:20.520
[electrical crackling continues]

863
01:03:18.029 --> 01:03:20.301
[music builds up]

864
01:03:25.040 --> 01:03:26.041
[thud]

865
01:03:26.125 --> 01:03:27.042
[music ends]

866
01:03:38.333 --> 01:03:40.916
[ominous music resumes]

867
01:03:44.208 --> 01:03:45.376
[Mercedes] Belén?

868
01:03:45.460 --> 01:03:47.125
Belén, please untie me.

869
01:03:48.080 --> 01:03:48.921
Belén?

870
01:03:49.500 --> 01:03:51.586
- Time to eat. - [Mercedes] No, no, no.

871
01:03:51.670 --> 01:03:53.416
- [Belén] Open your mouth. - No, no.

872
01:03:53.500 --> 01:03:54.499
Come on, open it.

873
01:03:54.583 --> 01:03:55.583
[sobbing] No.

874
01:03:58.333 --> 01:04:00.166
[Belén] Hey, you must eat

875
01:04:00.880 --> 01:04:03.624
so your eggs grow healthy and strong.

876
01:04:03.708 --> 01:04:04.549
What?

877
01:04:07.250 --> 01:04:08.625
You saw mine, didn't you?

878
01:04:11.708 --> 01:04:12.666
Poor things.

879
01:04:14.122 --> 01:04:15.875
No matter how much care I give them,

880
01:04:16.917 --> 01:04:18.500
they never get to be born.

881
01:04:19.452 --> 01:04:20.966
But she believes in you,

882
01:04:21.050 --> 01:04:22.625
that's why she brought you here.

883
01:04:23.375 --> 01:04:25.626
You still don't know who wrote that letter?

884
01:04:25.710 --> 01:04:27.324
Belén, this isn't like you.

885
01:04:27.408 --> 01:04:29.990
This isn't like you at all. That bug's driving you mad.

886
01:04:30.074 --> 01:04:30.916
I'm begging you.

887
01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:33.541
Just untie me so we can solve things.

888
01:04:33.625 --> 01:04:36.246
- [Belén] Open your mouth. - I promise you--

889
01:04:36.330 --> 01:04:38.208
- Open it! Now! - [Mercedes] No!

890
01:04:39.708 --> 01:04:40.956
[Belén] Good girl.

891
01:04:41.040 --> 01:04:41.917
There you go.

892
01:04:44.045 --> 01:04:44.953
[exhales]

893
01:04:45.037 --> 01:04:46.333
[Mercedes sobs]

894
01:04:46.417 --> 01:04:47.830
I know this is uncomfortable.

895
01:04:48.127 --> 01:04:50.416
But it will only be a few nights.

896
01:04:50.500 --> 01:04:54.167
Then I'll untie you and the three of us will live peacefully together here.

897
01:04:55.500 --> 01:04:57.333
At first, the nightmares are…

898
01:04:58.625 --> 01:04:59.956
horrible.

899
01:05:00.040 --> 01:05:01.923
But you get used to them after a while.

900
01:05:02.007 --> 01:05:05.083
She becomes part of your life and you lose the desire to leave.

901
01:05:06.069 --> 01:05:07.086
You'll see.

902
01:05:07.170 --> 01:05:09.583
Belén, untie me. I'm begging you. Please.

903
01:05:10.292 --> 01:05:12.792
- Eat up. - [Mercedes sobs] No, no, no. Please!

904
01:05:15.304 --> 01:05:16.667
[Belén] Just eat and sleep.

905
01:05:18.542 --> 01:05:19.383
[crying]

906
01:05:20.710 --> 01:05:23.375
[Mercedes] What's this, Belén? What did you put in it?

907
01:05:24.208 --> 01:05:26.458
Just something to help you sleep.

908
01:05:35.458 --> 01:05:36.583
She'll come for you.

909
01:05:44.833 --> 01:05:45.916
[door closes]

910
01:05:47.830 --> 01:05:49.667
[ominous music continues]

911
01:05:53.154 --> 01:05:53.995
[gasps]

912
01:05:59.000 --> 01:06:01.583
- [chittering] - [skittering]

913
01:06:03.864 --> 01:06:04.706
[chittering]

914
01:06:04.790 --> 01:06:05.632
[Mercedes] No.

915
01:06:05.716 --> 01:06:08.875
[gasps]

916
01:06:10.830 --> 01:06:12.291
[chittering]

917
01:06:12.375 --> 01:06:14.251
[Mercedes screams, sobs]

918
01:06:14.335 --> 01:06:16.417
[pulsing, ominous music]

919
01:06:18.460 --> 01:06:20.245
[skittering]

920
01:06:25.250 --> 01:06:26.496
[gasps]

921
01:06:27.284 --> 01:06:28.125
[gasps]

922
01:06:28.209 --> 01:06:29.050
[pants]

923
01:06:34.040 --> 01:06:36.167
[pulsing, ominous music continues]

924
01:06:38.792 --> 01:06:40.500
Look what she did to you.

925
01:06:55.000 --> 01:06:57.083
I won't let anything bad happen to you.

926
01:06:57.620 --> 01:06:58.792
[sobs, sniffs]

927
01:07:01.500 --> 01:07:03.292
I know you'll be born someday.

928
01:07:05.120 --> 01:07:08.042
[pulsing, ominous music continues]

929
01:07:27.290 --> 01:07:29.042
[music decrescendos]

930
01:07:48.500 --> 01:07:49.596
[cocks crossbow]

931
01:07:58.458 --> 01:08:01.323
Put that down and get back to the room

932
01:08:01.407 --> 01:08:03.456
if you don't want me to blow your head off.

933
01:08:03.540 --> 01:08:06.542
[vehicle approaching]

934
01:08:08.466 --> 01:08:10.167
[Belén screams]

935
01:08:10.251 --> 01:08:12.125
[dramatic music]

936
01:08:15.880 --> 01:08:18.126
- [Belén screams] - Get in there! Now!

937
01:08:18.210 --> 01:08:20.583
Get in there, Belén!

938
01:08:20.667 --> 01:08:22.292
Get the fuck in there!

939
01:08:23.574 --> 01:08:24.416
Get in!

940
01:08:24.500 --> 01:08:26.625
[Belén screams]

941
01:08:43.250 --> 01:08:44.833
[screams]

942
01:08:46.750 --> 01:08:48.250
[cries]

943
01:09:15.750 --> 01:09:17.458
Mercedes, what's going on?

944
01:09:18.251 --> 01:09:20.456
What happened? I heard a gunshot. Are you okay?

945
01:09:20.540 --> 01:09:22.917
[cries]

946
01:09:25.796 --> 01:09:28.836
I can't explain now. We must take Jaime to hospital. He's dying.

947
01:09:28.920 --> 01:09:30.500
Please, I need your help.

948
01:09:30.584 --> 01:09:31.746
[unintelligible]

949
01:09:31.830 --> 01:09:34.083
[dramatic music continues]

950
01:09:39.792 --> 01:09:41.208
[screams]

951
01:09:41.292 --> 01:09:43.542
- Grab the wheelchair. Jaime! - [distant scream]

952
01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:01.126
[Mercedes] Come on.

953
01:10:01.210 --> 01:10:03.665
Careful. Hurry!

954
01:10:05.920 --> 01:10:06.958
Start the truck.

955
01:10:13.167 --> 01:10:14.750
[Jesús] One, two, three.

956
01:10:17.918 --> 01:10:19.088
[gunshot]

957
01:10:21.292 --> 01:10:22.541
[music fades out]

958
01:10:23.253 --> 01:10:24.583
[Mercedes gasps]

959
01:10:29.375 --> 01:10:30.917
You've got some nerve.

960
01:10:32.875 --> 01:10:34.791
You thought you could come to my house,

961
01:10:34.875 --> 01:10:36.042
kill my babies,

962
01:10:36.917 --> 01:10:38.625
and get away with everything?

963
01:10:39.654 --> 01:10:40.496
Huh?

964
01:10:40.580 --> 01:10:42.417
[tense music]

965
01:10:45.830 --> 01:10:47.792
[breathes heavily]

966
01:11:14.500 --> 01:11:15.416
It was her, right?

967
01:11:16.917 --> 01:11:18.584
It's always been her.

968
01:11:21.170 --> 01:11:24.749
[Jaime breathes heavily]

969
01:11:38.380 --> 01:11:39.667
[music ends]

970
01:11:40.380 --> 01:11:42.292
[breathes normally]

971
01:12:17.833 --> 01:12:18.733
[whispering] Dad.

972
01:12:23.042 --> 01:12:24.167
Mercedes.

973
01:12:27.708 --> 01:12:29.084
You finally came back.

974
01:12:29.168 --> 01:12:30.541
[emotional music]

975
01:12:50.083 --> 01:12:51.999
Dad, we gotta leave. You're unwell.

976
01:12:52.083 --> 01:12:53.791
I must take you to a hospital.

977
01:12:55.125 --> 01:12:55.966
Yes, Dad.

978
01:12:58.750 --> 01:13:00.208
Take me inside.

979
01:13:00.292 --> 01:13:01.134
No, no.

980
01:13:01.218 --> 01:13:03.166
Please let's get out of here, Dad.

981
01:13:03.250 --> 01:13:04.833
I'm very tired.

982
01:13:07.042 --> 01:13:08.709
I want to go to bed.

983
01:13:10.292 --> 01:13:11.292
Please.

984
01:13:18.000 --> 01:13:19.333
[Mercedes] Watch your step.

985
01:13:31.534 --> 01:13:32.666
Mercedes.

986
01:13:32.750 --> 01:13:35.135
[music fades out]

987
01:13:36.083 --> 01:13:37.250
It's done for me.

988
01:13:40.750 --> 01:13:42.333
I need to rest.

989
01:13:45.407 --> 01:13:47.666
[Jaime] I just wanted to see you one last time.

990
01:13:47.750 --> 01:13:48.791
No, Dad.

991
01:13:48.875 --> 01:13:50.166
No, no, no.

992
01:13:50.250 --> 01:13:52.333
Help me, please.

993
01:13:53.458 --> 01:13:55.000
I don't want to go on.

994
01:13:58.250 --> 01:13:59.500
Are you sure?

995
01:14:05.750 --> 01:14:07.875
[sad music]

996
01:14:54.120 --> 01:14:54.961
Dad.

997
01:14:58.458 --> 01:15:00.625
I need to know…

998
01:15:01.375 --> 01:15:02.417
why you left

999
01:15:04.000 --> 01:15:06.875
and why you weren't there for me when I needed you most.

1000
01:15:08.500 --> 01:15:10.000
I'm sorry, sweetheart,

1001
01:15:11.125 --> 01:15:14.083
but the pain was too much to bear.

1002
01:15:14.917 --> 01:15:17.167
And though I really wanted to…

1003
01:15:19.792 --> 01:15:22.000
I could never forgive you.

1004
01:15:22.958 --> 01:15:23.999
Forgive me for what?

1005
01:15:24.830 --> 01:15:27.042
Julián's death.

1006
01:15:28.875 --> 01:15:30.916
My brother killed himself, Dad.

1007
01:15:33.708 --> 01:15:36.501
We told you that to protect you.

1008
01:15:36.585 --> 01:15:37.426
No.

1009
01:15:39.917 --> 01:15:41.036
You were in shock.

1010
01:15:41.120 --> 01:15:43.916
- No, that's not true. - You really don't remember it?

1011
01:15:44.000 --> 01:15:44.841
No.

1012
01:15:45.542 --> 01:15:46.625
It can't be true.

1013
01:15:48.042 --> 01:15:48.922
No.

1014
01:15:49.417 --> 01:15:50.792
Dad. Dad.

1015
01:15:52.875 --> 01:15:53.996
Dad.

1016
01:15:54.080 --> 01:15:55.417
[sobbing] No, Dad.

1017
01:15:56.710 --> 01:15:57.791
It's not true.

1018
01:16:10.960 --> 01:16:13.042
[brooding dramatic music]

1019
01:16:18.875 --> 01:16:21.000
[gasps]

1020
01:16:31.109 --> 01:16:33.004
[crying]

1021
01:16:41.290 --> 01:16:43.375
[cries]

1022
01:16:48.583 --> 01:16:50.541
[sobs]

1023
01:16:57.208 --> 01:16:59.125
[music builds up]

1024
01:17:43.917 --> 01:17:45.271
[music ends abruptly]

1025
01:17:52.750 --> 01:17:54.417
[dramatic music]

1026
01:17:57.167 --> 01:17:59.542
[sipping]

1027
01:18:26.454 --> 01:18:27.296
[gunshot]

1028
01:18:27.380 --> 01:18:30.625
[dramatic music continues]

1029
01:18:52.458 --> 01:18:53.500
[yelling]

1030
01:18:55.891 --> 01:18:58.608
[screaming]

1031
01:19:07.008 --> 01:19:08.559
[music fades out]

1032
01:19:08.643 --> 01:19:12.541
6 MONTHS LATER

1033
01:19:12.625 --> 01:19:13.887
[Luisa] Okay.

1034
01:19:13.971 --> 01:19:14.929
Finally.

1035
01:19:15.917 --> 01:19:17.864
I officially present it to you.

1036
01:19:18.583 --> 01:19:21.708
THE SECRET DAUGHTER

1037
01:19:28.333 --> 01:19:30.000
Nothing smells better than this.

1038
01:19:31.174 --> 01:19:32.583
This one came in today.

1039
01:19:32.667 --> 01:19:34.249
It will be published Friday.

1040
01:19:34.333 --> 01:19:36.124
No, Luisa. I don't like the critics--

1041
01:19:36.208 --> 01:19:40.171
"In The Secret Daughter, Mercedes Vega gets away from horror,

1042
01:19:40.371 --> 01:19:43.291
which established her as a writer, and presents a memoir

1043
01:19:43.375 --> 01:19:45.958
that's rooted in pure realism."

1044
01:19:46.670 --> 01:19:49.703
"This chronicle about her final days alongside her dying father

1045
01:19:50.125 --> 01:19:52.792
develops a simple but powerful narrative."

1046
01:19:53.500 --> 01:19:54.791
"The author bares her soul

1047
01:19:54.875 --> 01:19:58.820
to produce one of the deepest emotional stories

1048
01:19:59.417 --> 01:20:01.589
of all time."

1049
01:20:03.542 --> 01:20:05.292
What's wrong? Are you okay?

1050
01:20:06.750 --> 01:20:07.591
Mmm.

1051
01:20:09.522 --> 01:20:11.000
I need a minute.

1052
01:20:20.720 --> 01:20:22.887
[ominous music]

1053
01:20:27.583 --> 01:20:28.424
[gasps]

1054
01:20:41.208 --> 01:20:43.541
[retches]

1055
01:21:11.378 --> 01:21:14.179
[ominous music continues]

1056
01:21:30.080 --> 01:21:32.958
[rustle]

1057
01:21:38.380 --> 01:21:41.380
[rock music]

1058
01:23:10.292 --> 01:23:12.292
[rock music continues]

1059
01:24:59.617 --> 01:25:01.334
[music ends]

1060
01:25:02.305 --> 01:26:02.752
